# Where a loop writes objects made here alone, what is known of every OTHER object outlives its head. Who is another is an argument of identity by the order of making: what stood before the first such object was made cannot be it;
# of what came later nothing is known (Walker::isOtherThanRestOf()). Here the list that is read came later: it is the list made here, back through a veil: so it is not tested in front of the loop for a storage of numbers.
# THE LIE, testing=ValuesThatComeLaterAreTakenForOthersThanWhatIsMadeHere: it is taken for another: it is tested in front, and its elements are read as numbers all round the loop while the turn pushes a text into it.
# As built the answers look right even so, because a list into which a written text is pushed is born with boxed storage and fails that front. THE WRONG NUMBERS SHOW UNDER COLLECTIONS, where it is born otherwise:
